            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I think this ties in with whether we count the primary as a multicursor or not. Like with `]C`/`[C`, it leaves a cursor under the primary even if there wasn't one before (whereas `gQ` treats the primary not as a multicursor if I've understood your issue). I suppose it's to be decided if the same rationale should apply in both cases",
