            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@bobrippling: yes, exactly. \n\nSo while trying the new native multicursor implementation (which in general I find really well thought out) I found that not having the primary cursor treated as one of the multiple cursors to be awkward and counter-intuitive.\nI've been using multiple cursors for ages and other editors and the old vim-visual-multi plugin basically treat all 'cursors' the same when it comes to things like restoring the old state. ",
